        "original_id": "07b28a6d-0895-5f38-bbd0-1d83766b0831",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Saddleback Mountain, Sandy River Plantation, Rangeley, Franklin County, Maine\n- Organizations: Saddleback Maine, WRGY\n- Topics: ski resort, mountain geography, radio broadcasting\n\nFacts:\n- Saddleback Mountain is a mountain in Sandy River Plantation, Franklin County, Maine, near the resort town of Rangeley.\n- Saddleback Mountain is one of Maine’s highest mountains and one of fourteen in the state with more than 2,000 feet of topographic prominence.\n- Saddleback Maine is a ski resort on the northwestern slopes of Saddleback Mountain in Sandy River Plantation, near Rangeley, Maine.\n- Saddleback Mountain is the site of the Saddleback ski resort.\n- Saddleback Maine is Maine’s third largest ski area by trails, lifts, snowmaking percentage, vertical drop, and skier days.\n- Saddleback Maine has 66 trails, 5 lifts, 85% snowmaking coverage, and a 2,000-foot vertical drop.\n- WRGY has studios on Main Street in Rangeley and a transmitter atop Saddleback Mountain.",
